{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated","id":1229948,"title":"Exalted - have your PCs ever been defeated?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-25T00:25:52-07:00","id":1229948,"title":"Exalted - have your PCs ever been defeated?","content":"Has your exalted been defeated or lost before?<br /> <br /> I don't mean just a temporary setback. I mean a true defeat. Someone dies. The city you were defending is destroyed. The army you raised was crushed despite all your preparations. The mask of winters rampages all over Creation when you failed to stop him. <br /> <br /> If you did, then how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T02:38:35-07:00","id":1229957,"title":"","content":"Holy Shit yes, strap yourselves in cuz we are getting <i>explicative'd</i>.<br /> <br /> 2e. Playing in the Scavenger lands, Thorns, Celeron general East area. Here's the relevant players: Mako Li, and Eclipse with about 200 xp and 0 combat charms. Not even Dodge or Resistance. Nothing. All Social Fu, egregious use of charmshare and a fully paid up member of the Dangerously Free Thinkers Society. At this point he had Hollow Heart Transcendence, 20 Willpower, and could convince the rain not to fall. He could get seals to club themselves and have everyone thank him for it. The Mask of Winters was impressed at his beautiful cruelty once, and thats saying something.<br /> <br /> Mako is only not an beautiful bloodstain because he's best mates with the Zenith Balasar, the Twin-Tailed Comet. 7 feet of Super heavy plate, hate, and a warhammer that could be confused for a siege weapon. Balasar loves the UCS almost as much as he hates everything else. He has a loyal hound, size of a pony. That comes up.<br /> <br /> Paling around with these to is the mercurial Jason Chance, Dawn caste. If you could fuse Jack Sparrow and Dante into one person and give him the buster sword, you'd basically have Chance. He has all the self preservation of particularly clever brick (a suicidally overconfident brick with no will to live). Chance plays fast and loose with everything only because he hasnt found a way to be even less responsible. He has none of Mako's cunning or Balasar's stubborn refusal to believe actual reality. He likes to go nova with motes early and hard.<br /> <br /> Mako hates the Realm and the Great Houses because he's from one and was seen as a failure for not becoming a Terrestrial. Balasar found out that the Immaculate faith prohibits Sun worship so he decided that they had to be crusaded off the face of Creation and he was going to build that sol-damned crusade if it killed him, except even then he probably wouldn't realize he's dead because he's too stubborn. Chance just fucks around.<br /> <br /> For reasons that dont matter, the group acquired a Manse on a particularly good eldritch leyline, which should have been suspicious but when you are half mad with god-power that word stops having meaning to you. So for a round about way, Mako has put off the Wyld Hunt for months even though people are openly being solicited to renounce their livelihoods and rally to the Keep of the Glorious Sun and take up arms to overthrow the realm (did I mention that Mako is REALLY good at his job?). Well, the Mask of Winters is sick of us helping and then screwing him over by turns so he keikaku's the Wyld Hunt down on us before we are ready- this was part of his long term plan to screw over a gold faction sidereal, but that didn't matter yet.<br /> <br /> So what do you do when you are 4 Anathema and a few thousand unreasonably intense and possible zealotous jihad-crusaders staring down 50k troops and dozens if not hundreds of Terrestrials? Why, make a deal with a Fae Queen that isn't suspicious at all, of course! So she comes to our aid and the Solars and their hated foes the Deadly and Terrible Raksha swoop down on the Heroic and Probably Actually Righteous Wyld Hunt and go through them like wolves through a herd of Imperial Rabbits. The day is saved! Except that the Mask is pissed so his main enforcer/ Mako's technically-wife straight up declares that the Abyssal forces waiting in reserve are called in, reverse -RotK- ghost army style. Turns out that leaving all those thousands of bodies out for a few days on a night with no moon is a pretty good Build-Your-Own-Shadowlands kit (mercilessly squandered lives not included!). So now thats about to happen on, we'll say, wednesday and it's monday night.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that Fae Queen? she wants the ashes of the White Tree of Jewels, aka <i>the geomantic lynchpin for the entire god-damn East. </i>Yeah, cut it down, burn it, and give it to her. On Tuesday. Rock, meet apocalyptic hard place.<br /> <br /> Now, if you were sensible, you'd probably reach out to the remnants of the still-reinforcing Wyld Hunt and try to make a deal to avoid the Apocalypse. Or maybe you'd sell out to the Mask and let him use you to make a few favors and break some Divine kneecaps. Or even Entreat with the Fae Queen.<br /> <br /> So what does our intrepid hero Mako do? Suffers Limit Break from his plans not working out perfectly, of course! So if you had a callous disregard of literally all other beings in the multiverse and owed some ashes to a rainbow tart, well, goddamn, you'd get some ashes. So he did, and just figured if he puts it in a magic bottle that <i>She won't realize the deception. </i>Limit Breaks, kids, not even once. This does not go as planned, but instead of invading she decides, hey, I love Drama as much as the next Feather Boa'd Eldritch Larping Monstrosity, and she drops a truth bomb-<br /> <br /> When I said that Mask called in the Wyld Hunt? I lied. Mako was getting pretty deep in favors to that Abyssal trollop and he fucked up a secret optional objective on a mission, so <b>that</b> got the Wyld Hunt's attention. Ok, Mask was behind it because he's a douche, but still, this one falls onto Mako's shoulders <i>twice</i>. And the dominoes fall.<br /> <br /> The dead start rising, which spurs the Wyld Hunt to come down on us for round 2 with reckless abandon, because they think we are dishonoring their beloved dead and being baby-eater Anathema, and the dead start storm the Castle of the Sun and start killing off the human famrers-turned-warriors because it turns out a lot of buffs from 2e War are temporary. Oops. The Wyld Hunt arrive and their generals (the DBs) start Dynasty Warrior-ing the <i>shit</i> out of the humans and undead, making a strike team tip-of-the-spear move towards the keep as well. It should be noted, however, that this &quot;spear tip&quot; is more like &quot;almost 200 Terrestrial Exalted unified out of shear hate and cashing in all of their artifacts and resources&quot;.<br /> <br /> Things, don't, uh, go smooth.<br /> <br /> Balasar's hound, which can talk and is stronger than any 2 bears takes an arrow meant for Balasar and goes down. Balasar The Twin-tailed Comet lives up to his namesake and jumps around bringing the hammer down like a Hulk/Thor fanfiction up to 11. Chance has a great time up until he's backstabbed by that Abyssal scamp. And Mako, hoo boy. Mako.<br /> <br /> Mako, you see, never missed a chance to get a little advantage. So he learned his first and only life-preserving charmas part of the deal with the Fae Queen- Bastion of the Self (Heart). It's a Fae charm- essentially your body becomes dream stuff and obeys cartoon logic: he can't be harmed except by Charms and Magic Materials. He can't even be hurt by gravity. So Mako takes a bunch of arrows and swords into his body and &quot;falls&quot; to his &quot;death&quot; into a river. Go Heroes!<br /> <br /> There was another solar there and some empowered NPCs, but essentially the Solar PC is a sorcerer and she sorcery'd the dead back to dead and then smuggled herself away by boat. She was actually tasked by Balasar to Live and tell our allies about what happend.<br /> <br /> Any way, Mako emerges from the river at dawn and checks to make sure his clothes are fine (spoiler: he still looks picture perfect, the bastard). He finds Balasar clutching his beloved hound, who has been rasping out and trying to hold out for as long as he can. Balasar is inhumanly fucked up- he's only alive because everyone else was sure that he was dead. Hammer abandoned, armor sundered, riddled with spears and arrows. Blood around him so think its made the soggy ground into a proper british dinner. He can't say anything or even think, he's just thousand yard staring at his dog, who breathes out his last breath as the sun reaches them. Balasar is so stoic at this minute that he could have won a staring contest against a statue.<br /> <br /> Now, if you're Mako and your bread and butter is making deals and controlling people, you'd probably forget all that and just be stunned in silence at all the tragedy and failure and death and waste around you. But you are not Mako. So Mako decides that if this is his fault, it would be bad (A), that non-exalted have no intrinsic worth(b), and that, if you crunch the numbers, he's still saved more people up to this point then he got killed (c). He explains this to Balasar, because honestly Mako has no idea how deal with people who don't <i>want</i> things and have no vices.<br /> <br /> Balasar doesn't say anything. Balasar doesn't move. Balasar doesn't even breathe. And then Mako says that, on his life and word as a Solar, he will get Balasar a new dog.<br /> <br /> And Balasar hammers Mako so hard he literally flies into the <b><i>fucking stratosphere</i></b>.<br /> <br /> - - - -<br /> We ended the night on that note, all of us silent and drained. A real life year of work and plot and everything, all cataclysmically mismanaged, everyone beaten or scattered.<br /> The ST thanks us for the session. We get our coats on. Just as we are about to leave, he says<br /> <br /> &quot;You have 80xp to spend for next week. Let me know what your characters have done in the<b>Twenty Years</b> since the <u>Battle of the Fallen Sun</u>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 06-25-2018, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T03:15:41-07:00","id":1229964,"title":"","content":"Wow. <br /> <br /> That was... some thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T03:23:03-07:00","id":1229968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1229957#post1229957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> some crazy shit</div> </div> </div> </div>That was certainly a thing I just read.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T03:32:18-07:00","id":1229970,"title":"","content":"wow<br /> <br /> recently in the 2.5 southern alchy game I ST, I had my players raid a realm manse construction in Harborhead territory. There was a legion defending the place, but they did good prep-work, rallying nearby tribes into a coordinated raid on the place via mind-control of the tribal chiefs. (diplomacy via brain-probes)<br /> <br /> they had their sneaky alchy sneak in and assassinate the legion commander - and got really lucky, since a lot of DB defence charms can't stand up to celestial-tier essence...<br /> <br /> but later they ran into the local DB immaculate abbot, an essence 4 martial arts NPC.<br /> <br /> Now, I hadn't statted the guy to floor my players - but the party's two most combat optimized alchies got slapped around like wet noodles. This turned the raid into a running battle where they tried to escape, which they managed to by exploiting the fact that alchies don't really need to breathe - hiding out of sight at the bottom of a muddy river, or in nearby hastily-dug underground tunnels.<br /> <br /> it completely changed how I had imagined the fight going - but I just went with it, and my players learned an important lesson of just how small-fry they still are as essence 3 alchies in a world of far more seasoned wyld hunters and whatnot","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","user":"webkilla","date":". 06-25-2018, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T04:35:51-07:00","id":1229978,"title":"","content":"Hey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> , can I repost this on rpg.net?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T04:36:03-07:00","id":1229979,"title":"","content":"For 3e, We recently had such an encounter while wyld-shaping. The golden casket in the center of the hall started shuddering until its lid burst up, and dozens of spindly limbs crawled out, each bearing a smaller coffin. Toxic fumes billowed out of every one of them, and the buzzing sound overwhelming everyone was revealed to come from each coffin: whenever anything got close, the lid opened to reveal thousands of rows of teeth, grinding against each other, snapping at its prey. A behemoth.<br /> <br /> While ultimately the behemoth was killed and the wyld was (mostly) shaped, only 1 of the 4 solars survived, crippled, unable to even claim the prize they shaped the wyld for.<br /> The battlefield ended with a broken solar, a fuming broken casket, and several coffins shuddering, the buzz stopping slowly as blood leaked evidence of what happened to the others. The promises couldn't be kept. The goals were lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T04:39:46-07:00","id":1229981,"title":"","content":"Woah. Solars. Die to things in the wyld? <br /> <br /> How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T04:48:17-07:00","id":1229982,"title":"","content":"Grievous Injury, Curses, not having at least a chargen dawn's worth of exp dedicated to combat despite having about 90/60xp.<br /> When you are a brilliant sorcerer but the rest of your combat kit consists of &quot;I...have a sword&quot; you don't want to be in close range of the toxic meat grinder that ocasionally clinches as a counterattack.<br /> Its nasty 14 dice to clinch, control and savage while poisoning everything in range did most of the work. Two rounds in people started having wound penalties, and they spiraled out. Only the combat monster survived, by an inch of her life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T04:49:30-07:00","id":1229983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1229978#post1229978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> , can I repost this on rpg.net?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure. Spread the word. Just make sure you send me the link and credit me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T05:14:10-07:00","id":1229985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1229983#post1229983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, sure. Spread the word. Just make sure you send me the link and credit me.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?830372-Exalted-have-your-PCs-ever-been-defeated&amp;p=21964142#post21964142\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...2#post21964142</a><br /> <br /> done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T16:34:56-07:00","id":1230945,"title":"","content":"My Sidereal may be partially responsible for the death of the Unconquered Sun. The situation there is still developing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T17:01:21-07:00","id":1230949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1230945#post1230945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Sidereal may be partially responsible for the death of the Unconquered Sun. The situation there is still developing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dear Lord how do you accidentally kill someone that is perfectly invulnerable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T17:30:34-07:00","id":1230952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1230949#post1230949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Lord how do you accidentally kill someone that is perfectly invulnerable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is <i>perfectly</i> invulnerable, because perfection doesn't exist. As for killing someone with <i>im</i>perfect invulnerability, well, just look at Baldur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T19:06:57-07:00","id":1230978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1230949#post1230949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dear Lord how do you accidentally kill someone that is perfectly invulnerable?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's two answers to that.<br /> <br /> <b>Some character background- </b><br /> Stalking Cat is a Chosen of Secrets whose a master thief and heavily involved in organised crime.<br /> This goes all the way back to her backstory as an orphan in Cherak, she tried to blackmail a crime family called the Chang brothers after stealing one of their letters, they responded by abducting her little sister and the only family she had left. She realises that if she just gives the Changs the letter they'll both die so uses her initiative and gives it to a rival family motivating them to attack the Chang compound while she escapes with her sister.<br /> Unfortunately by the time this plan goes ahead her sister has already frozen to death and she's told she can't use her newfound power to simply murder the Chang brothers. She eventually puts a hit on them and it fools nobody, almost 20 years later what happened to her sister is still a source of anger and frustration to her.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we don't make deals with bad guys- </b><br /> Rakan Thulio approached her a while ago because he knows the little sister is a major point of vulnerability for her. She's expecting an offer of revenge and to tell him to take a hike, instead he offers to bring her sister back or more accurately introduce her to a version who had never died.<br /> Despite her skepticism she's interested in a way she never thought she could be and Thulio wants one little thing from her, a copy of the spell Unity of the Closed Fist. Easily done for her as she's one of the greatest thieves in existence. She also reasons that if Thulio has 5 Solars as patsies he's already a huge threat what's one spell going to do?<br /> <br /> <b>Our heart was in the right place, Ok?- </b><br /> We'd become aware of a group claiming to be the Unconquered Sun's demigod children at around this time, they'd been doing something which was causing older manses to explode and would've gone under our notice if they hadn't put Farhold in danger and then used an ally in Yu-Shan to get some of our group Audited. We decide to let their father deal with them, go to all this trouble to gain an audience with the Incana (this involved befriending a worm-like creature that may have been in Yu-Shan longer than the gods, traveling through a city's worth of mono-wire, fending off a forbidden god and winning a boat race) and tell the Sun his kids are making a mess to try and get his attention.<br /> His attitude to the whole thing is along the lines of &quot;Shit, not again&quot; even confesses to us that it's not the first time he's been a deadbeat dad. He's willing to meet with them and try to make this thing work. They end up agreeing to meet him at the Pinnacle of Mercy. We even get one of these previous children now elevated to a full goddess along for the ride to help mediate if necessary.<br /> We smelt a rat too late, Cat realised that Unity of the Closed Fist wasn't for a circle of Solars it was for the five of them. They combined into a being called The Second Sun and The Unconquered Sun, filled with remorse for his inaction and facing an opponent with several of his abilities was outmatched. We don't know if he survived or not but there's reason to believe that The Second Sun is on its way to Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 06-28-2018, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T02:12:16-07:00","id":1231052,"title":"","content":"Well, our games have never gone as bad as some of the previous stories, but a party of 5 solars started investigating a weird temple we found while on our way home from clearing 500 hungry ghosts out of a 1st age ruin... only to discover that we'd walked into the middle of some kind of demon summoning ritual (damn sidereals must have been screwing with fate for the timing to be that perfect)<br /> <br /> 20 solar limbs and 10 eyes entered the building. Only 12 limbs and 7 eyes left.<br /> - The two-sword wielding martial artist was missing a leg AND an arm (because he doesn't know when to stay down)<br /> - The archer no longer had an arm with which to pull back his string.<br /> - The weird &quot;I'll take all the strength-boosting athletics charms and not much else&quot; dawn lost an eye<br /> - And the almost brand new, barely 3 sessions old &quot;tank&quot; martial artist was burst like a bag when he got stamped on by a 30ft tall combat monster of a demon.<br /> <br /> I was the only character to walk out of that building intact, and that's cos I fly around on a cloud using social influence and kai attacks so I never got within range of it. <i>Technically we won</i>, but it certainly didn't feel like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T11:56:30-07:00","id":1231170,"title":"","content":"No. Not a single Exalt - of any type - has ever taken a single level of health track damage in any game I\u2019ve ever played in. We thought a character took two levels of lethal once in our very first game, but when we looked at the math again, we were wrong.<br /> <br /> At least in third edition we have many times taken initiative damage in withering attacks. So that gives a bit of a sense of danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T14:44:52-07:00","id":1231221,"title":"","content":"Not in direct combat, simply because the game is lethal enough that GMs are, reasonably, rather queasy about the fact that the difference between &quot;defeat&quot; and &quot;half the party is dead&quot; is kind of razor thin, so a lot of punches are pulled in direct combat scenarios.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, though, I would actually say that not only have I had Exalts who failed, I'm not sure I've ever had a character who unambiguously <i>succeeded</i>. &quot;Win the battle, lose the war&quot; and an ever growing precarious Jenga tower of barely-holding responsibilities you can barely keep from collapsing into a clusterfuck singularity is practically <i>the</i> definitory Exalted experience in my, well, experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T15:04:46-07:00","id":1231223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1230978#post1230978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[keikaku intensifies]</div> </div> </div> </div>Did Thulio at least keep his end of the deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T15:37:37-07:00","id":1231234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1231223#post1231223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did Thulio at least keep his end of the deal?</div> </div> </div> </div>He did. Though being reunited with her sister has had implications she is still coming to terms with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T19:19:31-07:00","id":1231283,"title":"","content":"In a game currently on hiatus, the Dawn got the crap beaten out of her and a good number of her mercenaries killed defending a questionably important objective after the Twilight decided to Limit Break and out them in the middle of a contested Dynast territory. The Wyld Hunt probably should have ended the campaign right there, but I decided to throw them a bone. They're in an uneasy truce with what few members of House Ledaal are protecting this profitable but remote Northern satrap, only because Ledaal (and their Ragara faux allies--fauxllies!) expects them to die on the front lines against the incoming invasion by the Bull. Things are just barely grim enough for them to make the offer, and, well...<br /> <br /> Enough of the Circle has personal history sufficiently antagonistic to the Bull that they're okay with this. (The Dawn is a <i>Tepet</i>)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> This one probably doesn't count. I played a parody character for a one-shot, once, a fumbling meathead named Legendary Brawler Sashimi, whose terrifying anima banner was a glorious, golden, flopping carp. It was so entertaining, we decided to give him a second session. Finding himself surrounded by venomous tree snakes towards the end of the time we had available, he launched into a battle trance, and I meticulously described how everything seemed to slow as he plotted the location and approach of each of his dozens of reptilian assailants. Only, you know, he wasn't that smart? Int 1, Wits 1? So the cinematic slow-mo scene cuts directly to him being covered in venomous snakes. It wasn't so much a battle trance as him kinda spacing out. He died immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T01:30:45-07:00","id":1231541,"title":"","content":"So, the very first Solar game I ever played is still going. I've been playing it for, oh... 8 years? 9? Once every three-four weeks, with a few hiatuses.<br /> <br /> We've had our successes: Stopping a number of wars, helping Harborhead chase out its Autocthonian invaders, uniting two warring dynasties, stopping demons rewriting time so they won the Primordial War, etc.<br /> But, honestly, as Celestials with hundreds and hundreds of XP (I had 750 by the end of 2nd ed, and we restarted 3rd with 200 +160 Solar xp), it's an extremely incompetent group.<br /> <br /> We've had plenty of failures and f***-ups.<br /> Especially at the beginning of the game (which, as I said, was the first Solar game most of the players had played)<br /> <br /> We started out on the steppe of Mon-Gul. We came together to investigate an ancient Solar ruin being excavated by the Realm, who'd made an alliance with local warlord Temujin, an enemy of my shaman's tribe.<br /> <br /> Our Zenith (or Dawn? I can't remember, it was 9 years ago) warlord on his yeddim decided to take on Temujin's army by himself. 1000 archers <b>shot him to death</b> at range before he could get close.<br /> My Twilight shaman, Shadow of Kings, challenged Temujin (a god-blood) to single combat. The god-blood<b> beat the crap out of me</b>, and I flared all over the place, revealing myself as a nice juicy Wyld Hunt target.<br /> <br /> So... we got on my Azure Chariot and fled 1000 miles west.<br /> Here we came to Sukhmet, an Egypt-expy country on the northern coast. We were joined by a local Night Caste, and started investigating a lost legion of Clockwork Soldiers left in small groups in different caves across the country.<br /> But our Dawn swordsman wandered off from the group and went to a different town (I don't remember why).<br /> We saw, miles away, his anima banner shoot up into the sky iconically... then suddenly get cut out.<br /> He'd been <b>killed by some mortal guards</b>.<br /> <br /> As our friend had just died and revealed there were Solars in the area... we got on my Azure Chariot and fled 1000 miles (or whatever) north to the Haslanti League.<br /> Here we joined a skyship expedition to the west to find some ancient ruins full of magitek or something.<br /> <br /> We had various adventures at different islands on the way. We defeated an ancient magitek intelligence, fled a living island that tried to eat everyone, etc, and finally discovered that the weird admiral who didn't care about his crews dying was a Pterok using illusions who just wanted us to take him to a lost city full of slumbering Dragon Kings in the west, who we woke up. We defeated a Realm army attacking them, so that was pretty successful.<br /> <br /> So, we then decided to fly off to Coral or something in our one remaining airship.<br /> We were trundling along when we were attacked by pirates, who used catapults to try and hole our balloon. They made a couple of small holes, and we began sinking. My bound Huraka had been blowing the ship along, and I thought we needed more lift, so I told them to &quot;<b>blow the ship <i>up</i></b>&quot;. So they blew our ship up, and its burning wreckage crashed into the sea.<br /> We then spent a month in a boat made of airship wreckage slowly rowing to Coral. (This included a fight with the ghost of a crewmember where we discovered no-one in the party had anti-spirit charms, which was awkward as he chased us around the ship. I managed to trap him in a salt ring eventually.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Tldr;</b></u><br /> The <b>Zenith</b> challenged an army by himself and <b>was shot to death at range</b>. We ran away.<br /> The <b>Dawn died fighting some random guards</b>. We ran away.<br /> We discovered we'd been tricked by a mad Pterok who'd got loads of people killed. We just went along with him anyway.<br /> During a fight with pirates, <b>I blew up our own airship</b> with poorly-worded commands<br /> <br /> <br /> But wait, there's more! That was just when the first ST was running it.<br /> Under our second ST:<br /> A<b> Lunar and two Solars were beaten up by mortals</b>. Once a Solar Martial Artist was beaten up by a single cook, who chopped the Solar's arm off with a meat cleaver.<br /> The <b>Zenith killed himself </b>because of things he'd done in limit break.<br /> A Dragon King outwitted us, summoned a horde of ghosts and zombies to wreck a capital city, and <b>killed our Essence 5 Slayer</b> in a Kaiju vs Kaiju fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Our most recent classic piece of incompetence is as follows:<br /> My Zenith was leading the other PCs across the Plateau of Leng to the Black Monastery to slay the Nephwrack who enslaved my brothers.<br /> To save time, we went through the evil forest. I told them not to investigate or get involved with weird stuff. An NPC wondered off in the night and vanished.<br /> Of course, they went and investigated. They found some weird trees with doors with weird symbols on. They pulled them open.<br /> This caused an eclipse. It stopped when they closed the doors.<br /> I told them not to open the doors. They opened them again. There was another eclipse.<br /> This made the local giant worm monsters angry. Also, the giant worm monsters ate our crew and airship.<br /> We managed to trick an evil sorcerer and took his chariot back home. We discovered that the eclipses had unleashed a horde of weird and evil forbidden monsters from under the ground, who'd killed thousands, including the sick pharoah.<br /> <br /> I should probably mention that the party's leader is a 16 year old naive boy-prince. His Lunar wife is 17 (they got married because he knocked her up while they were both drunk). My Lunar had Solar Bond 5 to him so went along with whatever he said. No offence to any teens on here, but I think we'd do better with more mature leaders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-01-2018, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T04:25:35-07:00","id":1231551,"title":"","content":"A solar lost to a mortal?<br /> <br /> Why didnt he not use his excellencies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T04:57:30-07:00","id":1231554,"title":"","content":"Well, when I lost to mortals (with two different characters) it was 2nd ed, and there were 5 of them, so one was making unexpected attacks.<br /> <br /> When Marak Hawkwind, Martial Arts master, lost a martial arts duel to mortal martial artists it's because he was fighting 3 or 4, didn't want to flare, and rolled badly.<br /> <br /> When Marak had his arm chopped off by a single cook with a meat cleaver... I'm not sure, tbh. I wasn't really paying attention. I think he thought &quot;a mortal could never defeat me!&quot; and didn't bother using excellencies. Or maybe he used them a bit, but rolled badly and the cook rolled really well? Not sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T05:21:34-07:00","id":1231558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1231551#post1231551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solar lost to a mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>These things happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T05:58:52-07:00","id":1231564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1231558#post1231558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These things happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>How.... unfortunate <br /> <br /> I should start a 'most ignoble/ hilarious way your exalted PC died'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T06:16:29-07:00","id":1231566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1231564#post1231564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should start a 'most ignoble/ hilarious way your exalted PC died'</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't <i>my</i> PC, but my first playgroup's Eclipse had made a binding bargain with a Fiend, resulting in him getting spirited away to the rest of the Fiend's coven in the Wyld. My character made it imperative that we go recover him, only for the Zenith to decide, once he learned what the <i>terms</i> of the agreement were, that he'd made too open-ended a promise, <i>and executed him on the spot</i>.<br /> <br /> I count this as a defeat for my PC, since his goal was to <i>save</i> the other PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T08:41:40-07:00","id":1231588,"title":"","content":"Another defeat occurred to me, though this was really just me, not the whole party.<br /> <br /> So, we were trying to make peace between the Essence 5 Solar Sorceress and her magical kingdom of magical people, and the Essence 5 Warlord who rules (sort of) the Djala.<br /> <br /> We eventually got them to agree to peace. Then we tried to get the Djala to help actually defend that kingdom from the coming Realm invasion, but their Warlord would rather see the mountain people die and then fight the Realm later. We pushed... and he then decided to go back on the peace deal, and invade the mountain kingdom so he could use it as a base to fight the Realm.<br /> <br /> At this point, it's been 4 sessions of negotiation and we've got nowhere. So my Night Caste decided to just go kill the Dawn. (His underlings were more reasonable, they were happy to defend the mountain kingdom in return for food shipments).<br /> <br /> I disguise myself, and sneak through the camp at 4am. I wanted to save my motes for the coming fight, so I just rolled my 10 dice for stealth, and got 5.<br /> The guard got 7.<br /> <br /> I tried rushing past him. He beat my roll.<br /> <br /> I eventually managed to hide. I tried sneaking past him and the battle group of guards who'd appeared. By this time I've battled him to within two range bands of the Dawn's tent. He rolls 9(!) successes to spot me. They charge after me and we have a big fight, while the Dawn slowly puts his armour on.<br /> <br /> He reaches us by the time I've killed 14 guys worth of battle group... but not this one Djala, who's stopped me disengaging 3 times.<br /> <br /> I hit the Dawn with a 53-dice decisive damage. He uses Adamant Skin and Ruin-Abasing Shrug, and takes 7 damage. I'm now crashed.<br /> He chops off my hand. My defence is now 2, due to Overwhelming and Wound penalties.<br /> The random Djala guard bops me on the head and knocks me out.<br /> <br /> I was then stripped and crucified.*<br /> <br /> That random Djala guard has now been promoted to one of the Dawn's top guys.<br /> <br /> *But this isn't a death. I escaped, was put on trial by other Solars, and was found innocent.<br /> <br /> I'd done 7 lethal damage and caused the Dawn to use a lot of his motes in our fight. He was supposed to be dueling a Zenith, naked, in the morning (she challenged him for being so unrighteous) but the other PCs had convinced her not to do it that night because they thought she'd just get herself killed.<br /> However, he did have the duel with the sorceress he'd arranged for the evening... she hit him with a Death Ray, he took 3 damage and ran away and hid.<br /> <br /> So, we managed to do 10 damage total to a Resistance-supernal Dawn... and he fled, roused his armies, healed all his damage, and the war is just beginning. Thus, I didn't really accomplish anything, and lost a hand. Oh, and he took my level 5 hearthstone. And the sorceress took my warstrider while I was hunting him down.<br /> <br /> (I've got them all back though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-01-2018, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T09:25:38-07:00","id":1231599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1231588#post1231588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another defeat occurred to me, though this was really just me, not the whole party.<br /> <br /> So, we were trying to make peace between the Essence 5 Solar Sorceress and her magical kingdom of magical people</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Magical people?<br /> <br /> How Magical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T14:28:19-07:00","id":1231656,"title":"","content":"They're all over 6 foot with elf-like fine features and pale skin. 1 in... 100(?)/1000(?) (I don't remember) is a fire mage who can shoot fire (as the Burning Name). They also have higher attributes than humans.<br /> They looked normal before, but were changed by going into a pool of liquid silver which changes them into their new form.<br /> There's also some scaly bureaucrat fire-mages.<br /> <br /> Also, the country has dragons, gryffons and golems.<br /> <br /> (The player's spent like 50xp on workings, maybe more. And her workings are cheap because she's an Adamant-Circle Sorcerer)<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying this, the Djala are magic too, as they all have Extended Lifespan and Exalted Healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T14:33:37-07:00","id":1231657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1231566#post1231566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't <i>my</i> PC, but my first playgroup's Eclipse had made a binding bargain with a Fiend, resulting in him getting spirited away to the rest of the Fiend's coven in the Wyld. My character made it imperative that we go recover him, only for the Zenith to decide, once he learned what the <i>terms</i> of the agreement were, that he'd made too open-ended a promise, <i>and executed him on the spot</i>.<br /> <br /> I count this as a defeat for my PC, since his goal was to <i>save</i> the other PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>This did make me chuckle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T14:41:10-07:00","id":1231661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1231564#post1231564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How.... unfortunate<br /> <br /> I should start a 'most ignoble/ hilarious way your exalted PC died'</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I once had a Fire Aspect who, during a countryside outing with the other Dynasts in Cherak, expressed his disinterest in Mariachi music. The mariachi-loving Mnemon decided this deserved a playful bop in the face with the back of his grand goremaul. He was a bit surprised when the Sesus bureaucrat's head exploded like an over-ripe melon.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also enjoyed the time the party had almost defeated some Sidereals, but the limit-breaking Twilight decided to duel the last one, and stabbed himself a bit so the fight would be fair. The Full Moon thought he was being an idiot (and didn't want him killing a hot girl Sidereal) so bashed the Twilight over the head with his moonsilver wrackstaff to knock him out... and killed him.<br /> Though, after laughing, I realised that I'd based the upcoming plot around the Twilight's previous incarnation (Ozandus Pol, ie Walker in Darkness), which was awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T21:55:35-07:00","id":1231723,"title":"","content":"<b>Big Picture</b><br /> My players learned that Lookshy (the city) was a Fae that was feeding off the fractured Solar demense left behind after Delheleshen\u2019s demise.<br /> <br /> The Fae in question he been working on a plan to escape creation but didn\u2019t have \u2018make sure the area doesn\u2019t explode behind me\u2019 task on its checklist. <br /> <br /> <b>The Sitch</b><br /> <i>Eclipse</i> has stolen into the city\u2019s underground caverns with <i>Dawn</i> in an attempt to bypass the outer prominaries and walls to meet with the general staff in secret. They are intercepted by Dian Yu who turns out to be an emanation and a battle ensues. <i>Eclipse</i> isn\u2019t built for a protracted battle and <i>Dawn</i> causes a lot of collateral damage in the first flurry, allowing Dian Yu to forcibly collapse the tunnels to try and bury them. <i>Eclipse</i> is urged to escape by <i>Dawn</i> so he can battle at full strength but Dian Yu is able to manipulate the tunnels to trap them in the demense heart - the backup pressure valves slot into place and traps <i>Eclipse</i> with no means of escape, a large orichalcum bulkhead separating the two circle mates. <br /> <br /> Cue tearful goodbyes as <i>Eclipse</i> urges <i>Dawn</i> to leave. <i>Dawn</i> refuses. <i>Eclipse</i> tries unnatural mental influence. <i>Dawn</i> resists. <i>Dawn</i> hammers into the bulkhead and tears it free, imperiling the entire city from the essence eruption. <i>Dawn</i> grabs <i>Eclipse</i> and tosses them out the door, slamming the bulkhead back in place and staying behind to hold it closed. <br /> <br /> <b>The Conclusion</b><br /> Lookshy now has a brand new Orichalcum statue of the Exalted who sacrificed themselves to protect the populace, not that anyone sees it or pays it homage, its still there in the Demense holding the door shut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T07:31:07-07:00","id":1231803,"title":"","content":"Ah, that's a good ending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T10:53:30-07:00","id":1232174,"title":"","content":"In my latest campaign, a bunch of citizens (and ice trolls, but that's irrelevant) were holed up in a part of Gethamane, hiding from Vodak. The PCs went into the tunnels to find anyone that had been taken by the &quot;monster&quot; (they had no idea who or what Vodak was), and found a group of &quot;survivors,&quot; which they led back to the citizens holed up. They then left again to find and kill the monster, which, to be fair, they did. <br /> <br /> However, when they got back, they discovered that the &quot;survivors&quot; were merely some of Vodak's unholy spawn, and they had killed most of the remaining huddled citizens and some of the ice trolls. They left Gethamane, sorcerously sealing the doors behind them, and declared it an unholy, cursed place where none should tread. <br /> <br /> They never even learned about the Reality Engines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:08:07-07:00","id":1236838,"title":"","content":"If I need a defeat or character death for a story, I'll try to arrange it with the player beforehand. Getting buy-in helps a lot. When the time comes, I can raise a few story flags, and my player (who'll usually be pretty enthusiastic about going out with a bang) will be ready to face it head-on. <br /> <br /> Then again, we did have that Cyberpunk game where our team medic kept rolling 1's and battlefield-malpracticed the team into the ground. Not Exalted, but oh the memories. <br /> <br /> And then there was a Mage game where our Kung-Fu-Chick <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(tm)</span> got caught by the Technocracy and started looking up what her stats would be as a Wraith.<br /> <br /> Ha!<br /> <br /> Strictly in Exalted, our defeats and setbacks have needed to be arranged beforehand. Often, Exalted seems to get into a victory-or-death mindset, fighting to the last bitter breath. Talking it out with the players beforehand, I can get across that I'm setting up an enemy that's unstoppable today, but that they can gain power and defeat in due course of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T14:12:33-07:00","id":1236897,"title":"","content":"My first Exalted game spanned 7 years and 1e to 2e. <br /> - we accidentally set off a soulbreaker orb in lookshy<br /> - accidentally killed Autochthon and turned him into a neverborn<br /> - turned a god, a sidereal, and multiple animals into demons because our Dawn caste had a demonic hand<br /> - found out another circle of Solars was actually trying to FIX creation while we were dicking around trying to collect artifacts and wealth<br /> - screwed over said other circle of Solars <br /> - found out at the end we were actually the villains of our STs game the whole time....so maybe these aren't actually defeats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24418-dracheau","name":"Dracheau","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T06:19:10-07:00","id":1237111,"title":"","content":"Our group cannot agree if this counts as a defeat or not, which I think makes it count by itself:<br /> <br /> Our Circle of four (plus one) essence 2 Solars had found the legendary lost city of Rathess, freed it from the tyranny of Filial Wisdom and his god Han-Tao, (read: we beat the shit out of them and sent them packing), and reawakened the last sentient Dragon King. When the Storyteller asked what next, we were at loss for words.<br /> That is, until our circle's glorious leader Rade (a shirtless mix of Karl Marx and the dudes from Jersey Shore) had a suggestion: &quot;We're going to have THE BEST PARTY EVER.&quot;<br /> <br /> Having no better ideas, the rest of us agreed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next several sessions were spent in preparation: we contacted the Court of Seasons, asked if they could have one of their parties in Rathess, and eventually became party managers for one of them. (Forgot which, a giant chill treedude.)<br /> My character, sorcerer-bureaucrat Eclipse, Cous-Cous is busy doing basically everything: he summons demons to act as chefs, security and entertainment. He uses Flawless Brush Method to make enough invitations for everyone. (We distribute them in rolls, like toilet paper.) He settles logistics by creating a portal to connect Rathess and our burgeoning nation Radeland together. (Did I mention, the invitations contain exact directions to a state ruled by Anathema?)<br /> Meanwhile our crafter makes decorations, our glorious leader is busy having coitus with his trophy wife, our Zenith Anbir lures every Emperor Sloth within a hundred miles in and makes cocktail bits from their meat - thus devastating their entire population - and our Night, Cael, negotiates a narcotics deal with some Fae infesting one of Rathess' obelixs. While probably keeping watch on all of us, the paranoid clod.<br /> Basically our Circle only gathers together to do something necessary, yet highly irresponsible - like diverting the dragon lines of a prosperous neighbor city-state, so we could grow enough grain for all the cakes for the party\u2026 and we only end up buying them from the aforementioned, now approaching a hunger-crisis, neighbor, when none of us know how to bake.<br /> <br /> Our Circle soon figures out that none of us actually have the necessary skills to organize a party! (Rade and Anbir were charismatic enough to convince the gods, but had no management skills whatsoever. My bureaucrat's abilities were overstretched - he actually had zero Bureaucracy charms, so he had to get by with mere Excellency.)<br /> In Character and Out of Character we begin to realize that the party is going to be a disaster.<br /> <br /> That is, until Five Days Darkness, a total bro, answers our RSPV and offers to help us. We gladly accept his help.<br /> Some time later the treedude visits to check, how planning is going.<br /> ...<br /> He hates everything he sees. He wants the demons out, wants to touch nothing made by the fae, and loathes the idea of secret underground gladiatorial pits.<br /> He cannot stand Five Days Darkness and commands us to deny entry if he comes.<br /> Only our glorious leader's charisma saves the situation: Rade convinces the god that plants and trees are on their way and that the demons won't be there when the party begins. Cous-Cous makes a note to disguise the demons as locals.<br /> <br /> Also, our open invitation attracts a small Wyld hunt (actually a group of mercenaries hoping to cash in our bounty), which we luckily repel before the serious guests show up. Then there's a small problem of the portal connecting to Yu-Shan with every 1001<sup>st</sup> passage, but that is fixed with some clear instructions.<br /> The guests begin to arrive, and nothing is on fire\u2026 yet.<br /> The opening ceremony actually goes well. The gods of Rathess make a touching speech, more &quot;adventurous&quot; gods are discreetly directed towards the fighting pits, while squares like the treedude remain unaware on the ground level. Five Days Darkness is surprisingly understanding. He offers to stay on the sidelines - but we persuade him to stay. Can't leave a bro hanging.<br /> We even get an emissary from distant Thorns: a gothy looking kid named Typhon. Has an odd fashion sense, but seems like a good and trustful fella.<br /> After the first day, we begin to think we actually might make it.<br /> <br /> Then we wake up to see all our decorations burning.<br /> Or, to be exact, we smell them first. It's not showy burning with flames and stuff, but more like quiet smoldering.<br /> We begin to search the city, looking for the source of this.<br /> Everything is going to shit and the chaos causes Cous-Cous to Limit Break. (First of the chronicle, woo!)<br /> And, unfortunately, he's the first to find the distruption:<br /> Cue Jealous Saffron Rage, a some kind of hate elemental, making his appearance.<br /> <br /> Interlude: Now, to understand this turn of events, I need to tell your about a story earlier in our campaign: we were just settling in Radeland, when we visited a neighboring town. Turns out that an evil mortal sorcerer used the townsfolk as a hate generator for his schemes.<br /> A couple of hours later, the village is on fire, the townsfolk forcefully relocated to a less hate-generating area, and the sorcerer is our prisoner. When we interrogate him, he threatens us with his master's, Jealous Saffron Rage's, wrath.<br /> The prisoner is executed by the overzealous Night (he has a thing for abusers of authority), before Cous-Cous gets to make a deal with him.<br /> <br /> Back to Rathess: Rage has returned with a revenge in mind.<br /> Except that the now Deliberately Cruel Cous-Cous is more interested in negotiation.<br /> &quot;I'm dreadfully sorry about your servant. How about we give the one who killed him to you in a trade? Sounds only fair that he'd become your new slave.&quot;<br /> However, the rest arrive before the negotiation gets to proceed.<br /> &quot;We'll handle this, Cous-Cous!&quot; Rade commands, &quot;you go and make sure the party goes well and EVERYONE HAS FUN.&quot; Cous-Cous obeys.<br /> JSR then unleashes a hate plague - which affects everyone present (none of them had much Integrity) and forces them to act according to a strong negative emotion: Anger, Rage, Jealousy, etcetera. Like a smaller Limit Break.<br /> <br /> So, Anbir begins to act on his Defining Principle of &quot;Terrestial Gods are lazy jerks&quot;. He activates his fear aura (Hideous merit + all the Intimidation charms) and begins to chase the gods out.<br /> &quot;Come on, the party's over! EVERYONE OUT!&quot;<br /> Cael picks up one of the gods, takes her to a cellar and begins to torture the poor soul who was only looking for some good time. She doesn't confess. She wants to, but doesn't know what she's accused of.<br /> (I don't know what Intimacy he was channeling, but it doesn't give a good impression of him.)<br /> Rade channels his rage towards Jealous Saffron Rage. He manages to banish JSR by himself.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, you might remember just a moment ago Cous-Cous was commanded to make everyone have fun\u2026 or else.<br /> He sees people fleeing the city. (The gods could just Hurry Home, but their mortal attendants had to flee to the jungle.)<br /> This would not do. This wouldn't do at all.<br /> So Cous-Cous took command of some of his summoned Blood apes (party security) and made them round up everyone trying to leave in one location.<br /> Then they were ordered to dig pits. Once ready, everyone was thrown into the pit. Then the Blood Apes stood guard, and everyone trying to leave the pit or not having enough fun was poked with spears.<br /> These so-called partyholes are infamous even today.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Rade has managed to calm down both Cael and Anbir. Together they seek Cous-Cous and see what he has done.<br /> &quot;What have you done?!&quot; Cael yells with a manic grin on his face.<br /> &quot;I did what was NECESSARY! None of this would have happened, if you'd become slave like you DESERVED!&quot; Cous-Cous replies.<br /> Which blows up the bomb. Half our Circle has Slavery as their Limit Trigger. (This encounter causes Anbir and Cael to have their Limit Breaks in the two following sessions.)<br /> Cael attacks Cous-Cous, who defends himself.<br /> They would have killed each other (read: Cael would have eviscerated Cous-cous), unless Anbir and Rade hadn't wrestled them both down.<br /> This also makes Cous-cous' Break end. He mumbles something like an apology and admits he might have done some hasty things, but that he had been under a lot of stress lately.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, the party is ruined because most of the guests are now deathly afraid of the organizers. To save at least something, we make a quick plan with 5DD: we stage a fight where he arrives to banish the evil Anathema and free the people from the pits. Rade loses a mock-battle and gives a speech about 5DD's noble virtues and how he cannot possibly do evil in the face of them.<br /> We run away, 5DD saves the party and everyone wins. (Except, well, most people present.)<br /> 5DD is redeemed in the eyes of the people (tho the Court hates him even more) and the Final Dragon King dons the crown of Rathess.<br /> <br /> Our takeaway? We made a lot of powerful enemies in the Court of Seasons. We wasted most of our resources, announced our presence (and both of our kingdom's locations!) to the Wyld hunt, and made dubious promises of cooperation to a deathknight.<br /> Jealous Saffron Rage is still loose and we have no idea, if he's satisfied with this. One session later Cael limit breaks and Cous-Cous dies in a fight against a soulsteel golem (no one can prove it was Cael). Anbir burns Cous-cous' corpse and uses the Zenith anima power to take on his Intimacies - turns out the creep held only hate and contempt for the rest of the Circle.<br /> We get trapped in the Underworld, and Anbir limit breaks. The ghosts crown him king.<br /> My new character cannot believe these schmucks she found could survive even a day alone and joins their Circle.<br /> <br /> So was it a defeat?<br /> The players all thought it was hilarious, and we kinda wanted it to happen.<br /> The Solars are either too stupid or too proud to admit any of this was their fault, and consider it a great success.<br /> Our Storyteller has yet to go insane.<br /> <br /> I want to call it one, but I can't find the reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","user":"Taleksi","date":". 07-20-2018, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T10:42:57-07:00","id":1237191,"title":"","content":"Oh man, that was brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T13:02:18-07:00","id":1245170,"title":"","content":"Any time there was a defeat by mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T13:32:53-07:00","id":1245174,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned earlier, my Twilight was once surrounded by 5 tribesmen who beat him unconscious. But this was in 2nd ed, when the 5th guy got to make unexpected attacks, and I didn't have any Dodge charms. It'd be much easier to win in 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> My friend's Eclipse martial artist got beaten by a cook with a cleaver. Not to death though.<br /> <br /> He also, years ago, had a Dragonblood killed by mortals. The issue with fighting with mortals, is people think &quot;oh, they're only mortals, I don't need to bother spending Essence&quot;, but without that, you're actually not really better than them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T13:38:56-07:00","id":1245176,"title":"","content":"There is a reason why Mortals are banded in battlegroups. It doesn't really suit Exalted-style to lose to a mortal. With couple of funny exceptions of course.<br /> That being said, some of my characters would've been in trouble with a battlegroup if the group's Single Point-stylist hadn't been around.<br /> Mortals are never meant to defeat the Exalted. Just to provide interesting challenges, not necessarily in battle. World has enough supernatural adversaries to keep it interesting anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11221-turtleking","name":"Turtleking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:24:10-07:00","id":1245200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Turtleking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245176#post1245176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a reason why Mortals are banded in battlegroups.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>characters who aren't narratively important enough to be represented individually yet are still relevant enough to the fight to represent at all</i>\u200b are banded in battle groups. Many of these will be mortals, but hardly all of them must be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Turtleking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245176#post1245176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really suit Exalted-style to lose to a mortal.<br /> Mortals are never meant to defeat the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm forced to disagree with you pretty hard, here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T17:59:56-07:00","id":1245251,"title":"","content":"I don't want to play in a game where I can't get in a massive barfight with a bunch of other pirates, only to have the bartender knock me out with a wine bottle to the back of the head when she sees the mess I've made of her establishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T17:59:59-07:00","id":1245252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245174#post1245174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned earlier, my Twilight was once surrounded by 5 tribesmen who beat him unconscious. But this was in 2nd ed, when the 5th guy got to make unexpected attacks, and I didn't have any Dodge charms. It'd be much easier to win in 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> My friend's Eclipse martial artist got beaten by a cook with a cleaver. Not to death though.<br /> <br /> He also, years ago, had a Dragonblood killed by mortals. The issue with fighting with mortals, is people think &quot;oh, they're only mortals, I don't need to bother spending Essence&quot;, but without that, you're actually not really better than them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you have. The only thing you really need against a mob is something that removes onslaught penalties and you'll never be hit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T20:10:30-07:00","id":1245297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245252#post1245252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on what you have. The only thing you really need against a mob is something that removes onslaught penalties and you'll never be hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Never&quot; is a bold claim. If you've maxed-out your Defense and you're up against a small, untrained mob, it's certainly <i>unlikely</i> (though not <i>impossible</i>, since NPCs still benefit from double-10s) that you will be hit even if you don't use Charms other than penalty-removers. But mortal dice pools in Core go up to 11 dice for Elite Troops, and Size bonuses to Attack go up to +5. A <i>very large</i> mob, or even a small unit with proper training, <i>will</i> hit an Exalt who isn't using Charms other than penalty-removers, even if they've got great base Defense. And a Size 3+ Battle Group with good dice pools which is the beneficiary of Order Actions can potentially even threaten Exalts who <i>are</i> using defensive Charms. The Size bonus to Soak can even insulate them somewhat from reprisal, unless the Exalts have Artifact Weapons, high enough Initiative to make a Decisive Attack (circumventing Soak), or some other answer to high Soak.<br /> <br /> Mortal Battle Groups aren't a <i>lethal</i> threat to <i>most </i>Solars, but that doesn't mean they can't be a threat at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T20:36:59-07:00","id":1245304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245297#post1245297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a Size 3+ Battle Group with good dice pools which is the beneficiary of Order Actions can potentially even threaten Exalts who <i>are</i> using defensive Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the wood DB skald rolls 22 successes on her command action you bet her size 4 elite drill cavalry is going to put in some hurt.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T22:11:52-07:00","id":1245335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245304#post1245304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the wood DB skald rolls 22 successes on her command action you bet her size 4 elite drill cavalry is going to put in some hurt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not at all mortals only.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T22:15:09-07:00","id":1245336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245297#post1245297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Never&quot; is a bold claim. If you've maxed-out your Defense and you're up against a small, untrained mob, it's certainly <i>unlikely</i> (though not <i>impossible</i>, since NPCs still benefit from double-10s) that you will be hit even if you don't use Charms other than penalty-removers. But mortal dice pools in Core go up to 11 dice for Elite Troops, and Size bonuses to Attack go up to +5. A <i>very large</i> mob, or even a small unit with proper training, <i>will</i> hit an Exalt who isn't using Charms other than penalty-removers, even if they've got great base Defense. And a Size 3+ Battle Group with good dice pools which is the beneficiary of Order Actions can potentially even threaten Exalts who <i>are</i> using defensive Charms. The Size bonus to Soak can even insulate them somewhat from reprisal, unless the Exalts have Artifact Weapons, high enough Initiative to make a Decisive Attack (circumventing Soak), or some other answer to high Soak.<br /> <br /> Mortal Battle Groups aren't a <i>lethal</i> threat to <i>most </i>Solars, but that doesn't mean they can't be a threat at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally every exalt NPC that I have seen with any decent investment in combat has some artifact weapon. It's at the point where I just assume every exalt somehow has an artifact weapon. Even with 16 dice that doesn't guarantee you'll pierce 9-11 defense. You could use more charms to guarantee a win but with just a simple single charm, you almost guarantee a win. With a few more, it's statistically impossible to lose. That's why greater threats are needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-13-2018, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T05:13:38-07:00","id":1245404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245335#post1245335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not at all mortals only.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sure(it *can* happen with a mortal, but it's basically a small miracle I agree). With but a great baseline defense (let's say 9 for a stunt 2 max base pool with a daiklave). 10 dice have a 3.6% chance to hit. 14 dice...19%<br /> A size 2 fyrd has 10 dice. A good mortal commander bridges the gap to 14 dice 30% of the time.<br /> Easily achievable for a standard &quot;here's a mob to fight you&quot; situation. No threat to a full circle, nor the dawn monster, but not trivially defended either, especially if you consider the whole circle won't likely have 9 defense for cheap .<br /> <br /> A couple heroes with exceptional equipment are a similar threat with the onslaught negator.<br /> <br /> Against the elite, so to say, you can expect the battle group to sport some 11 dice. A size 2 unit with a similarly powerful commander will on average throw 18 dice on you, a 43% chance to hit defense 9.<br /> Can't ignore that.<br /> <br /> Throw in a proper wyld hunt dragon and by now there's so much Magnitude you can't afford risking a decisive because it will live for a few rounds and you'll be in danger of crashing, by which point you will have to <b>slog</b> through the numbers. Unless you're a resistance or athletics supernal with their respective white reaper doom combos, that is, but those two builds never taking damage or oneshotting sinze 3 battle groups is mostly intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T05:27:02-07:00","id":1245409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245336#post1245336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with 16 dice that doesn't guarantee you'll pierce 9-11 defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience you don't really need to.<br /> Most Exalts generally don't boost their defence that much up front against an enemy without a dice adder and tend to want to conserve their motes for the next potential problem, which can lead to costly mistakes in the short-term. I've never seen anyone die because of this mind you, but I've seen health levels get lost that didn't need to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T06:17:47-07:00","id":1245432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245336#post1245336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally every exalt NPC that I have seen with any decent investment in combat has some artifact weapon. It's at the point where I just assume every exalt somehow has an artifact weapon. Even with 16 dice that doesn't guarantee you'll pierce 9-11 defense. You could use more charms to guarantee a win but with just a simple single charm, you almost guarantee a win. With a few more, it's statistically impossible to lose. That's why greater threats are needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not white-rooming. I didn't lay out the whole situation earlier because it wasn't a pure mortal encounter (they had both Dragon-Blooded backup and a little Might, which certainly helped), but in the current PbP game I'm running, I saw my PCs struggle for a bit against a Battle Group of Elite Troops, due largely to the Size buff to Soak and the fact that only two out of five of the then-current PCs were using artifact weapons. (A third had access to artifact stats on Silver-Voiced Nightingale kiais, but those aren't her primary weapon.) A Decisive attack was what finally wiped out the Battle Group.<br /> <br /> And the maximum baseline defense anybody's toting around is 8, by my reckoning (Dex 5, Ability 5, and Specialty makes 6, Medium Weapon gives 7, and you can basically count on Stunt 1 for 8). Anything beyond that takes effort (descriptive effort, Willpower, or Charms). The composition of my group of PCs has shifted a little, and now four out of five do have access to artifact weapons (counting the Nightingale), but even now only two out of five of my PCs have maximum Defense.<br /> <br /> As I said before, I'm not saying that mortals are a <i>lethal</i> or <i>dire</i> threat to Solars, because no, they aren't. But if those Solars aren't heavily combat invested or at least willing to use defensive Charms, it's statistically plausible for mortal Battle Groups to land hits sometimes, and Battle Groups with high Soak can potentially take a few hits in return before folding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T06:30:48-07:00","id":1245437,"title":"","content":"Which is basically what they should be doing, for a genre-appropriate and fun game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T21:06:24-07:00","id":1245744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229948-exalted-have-your-pcs-ever-been-defeated?p=1245437#post1245437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is basically what they should be doing, for a genre-appropriate and fun game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... when I said defeated by a mortal, I meant out maneuvered. The Dawn is pretty darned powerful? He gets tricked and misdirected, and sent to kill some rich dude's enemies. When he finds out and comes for revenge, the dude commits suicide, meaning that he's now out of his reach, content in the knowledge that he dragged his foes down with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}